# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]   (no dollar/backtick in the text)
register_gate "tests/test_rerun_fork_safety.py" "RERUN-FORK-SAFETY GATE: PASS" "rerun fork safety" "the check_suite/check_run rerequested replay carries base.repo + base.sha + the neighbor-refresh suppressor, so a re-run on a FORK PR is detected as a fork (redacted, no base-repo in-flight info leak), keeps symbol-level precision, and does not fan an N-by-M neighbor-refresh storm" "Locks the round-1 audit fix (A4-F1/F2/F5): the synthetic 'synchronize' payload built for a re-run (check_suite/check_run rerequested) used to be base:{ref} only. WHAT THAT BROKE: (1) FORK INFO LEAK -- no base.repo meant base_repo_id=None so the synchronize path computed is_fork=False; an EXTERNAL contributor pressing Re-run on a fork PR's Veripsa check then got the FULL non-redacted body (the base repo's OTHER in-flight PR identities and paths) posted on their PR; (2) VERDICT REGRESSION -- no base.sha meant the finer-collision freshness read was skipped, so a re-run silently degraded to a coarser file-level verdict; (3) NEIGHBOR STORM -- no suppressor meant each replayed PR fanned a neighbor-refresh across the whole in-flight set (N-by-M GitHub posts on one click). The fix extracts a pure _rerun_replay builder that carries base.repo, base.sha and _veripsa_no_neighbor_refresh. This gate drives that builder directly (PURE, no DB, no GitHub) and asserts: base.repo / head.repo / base.sha / the suppressor are present; the SAME is_fork formula the synchronize path uses now returns True for a fork PR and False for a non-fork (no over-redaction); and a sparse PR object degrades to empty objects without crashing while unknown fork identity fails closed to the redacted surface. Content-free (ids/shas/paths shapes only, no code bodies)." 10
